# ============================================================
# .gitignore — hardened for financial material
#
# This repository is public; the machine that develops it holds real financial
# data. The failure mode is a real statement or export committed by accident and
# living in git history forever. Real state lives OUTSIDE every worktree, in the
# private data home — docs/DESIGN.md, "Public code, private data" — so most of
# what follows is a second line of defence rather than the first.
# ============================================================

# --- Real financial data: never committed ---
# These are no longer repository directories at all. Real state lives outside
# every worktree, in the private data home ($PURSER_HOME, else
# $XDG_DATA_HOME/purser) — docs/DESIGN.md, "Public code, private data". Nothing
# purser writes can land here any more.
#
# The rules stay anyway. A redundant ignore rule costs nothing, and a human who
# drops an export into ./data/ out of eight months of habit is exactly the case
# a redundant rule is for.
/data/
/reports/

# --- The real account registry ---
# config/accounts.example.yaml is tracked; the real accounts.yaml is personal
# (it names where the captain actually banks) and lives in the private config
# overlay, $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/purser/accounts.yaml.
/config/accounts.yaml

# --- Credentials and environment ---
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
credentials*
secrets*

# --- Statement / export formats, wherever they land ---
# tests/fixtures/ holds SANITIZED samples only and is re-included below.
*.csv
*.ofx
*.qfx
*.qif
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.pdf

# --- Local databases ---
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# --- Python / tooling artefacts ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# --- OS and editor noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# --- Explicit re-inclusions ---
# gitignore is last-match-wins, so these MUST stay at the bottom.
# Only sanitized fixture data may be re-included here.
!/tests/fixtures/
!/tests/fixtures/**
